# What the TUI needs to present and run this industry. No engine code changes per industry.
INDUSTRY|Education
PROCESS|Faculty Admissions and Bursary Processing
DEFINITION|data/education_admissions.workflow
ABOUT|A faculty receives an application, verifies the applicant against the national ID registry, reviews it academically, then issues an offer or a regret letter. Bursaries are approved at a level set by the amount and paid through the bank.
EXPECTED|The application closes with an offer (and a paid bursary if approved) or a regret letter. An identity failure rejected at intake ends the whole instance.
PARTICIPANT|edu-clerk|Lerato Khumalo|Admissions Clerk
PARTICIPANT|edu-officer|Sipho Ndlovu|Admissions Officer
PARTICIPANT|edu-eng|Dr Priya Pillay|Engineering Reviewer
PARTICIPANT|edu-hum|Dr Johan Botha|Humanities Reviewer
PARTICIPANT|edu-aid|Thandi Mahlangu|Financial Aid Officer
PARTICIPANT|edu-mgr|Ayanda Zulu|Faculty Manager
PARTICIPANT|edu-dean|Prof Nomsa Sithole|Dean
PARTICIPANT|edu-fin|Michael Jacobs|Finance Clerk
INPUT|surname|Applicant surname|Mokoena
INPUT|idNumber|SA ID number (seeded: 0501015800087 Mokoena, 4808105009083 is deceased)|0501015800087
INPUT|faculty|Faculty (Engineering or Humanities; anything else goes to the Admissions Officer)|Engineering
INPUT|amount|Bursary amount in rands (up to 50000 Aid Officer, 150000 Manager, above that Dean; gateway limit 100000)|45000
INPUT|accountNumber|Bank account, 9 to 11 digits|123456789
INPUT|branchCode|Branch code|250655
INPUT|reference|Payment reference|BURSARY-2026-001
